        <!-- SECTION 1: What Makes an Inverter Generator Different -->
        <div id="how-inverters-work" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. What Makes an Inverter Generator Different
          </h2>

          <p>
            A conventional generator's alternator has to spin at a fixed 3,600 rpm to produce 60 Hz power, regardless of whether you are running a well pump or charging a phone. Its output quality is a direct function of that speed holding steady, and its noise is a direct function of running flat out all the time.
          </p>

          <p>
            An inverter generator breaks that link. It produces raw AC at whatever engine speed is convenient, rectifies it to DC, then electronically synthesizes a clean 60 Hz sine wave from that DC. Because output frequency no longer depends on engine speed, the engine can idle down when demand is low. Three consequences follow, and they are the entire reason the category exists.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Clean Power</h3>
          <p>
            Total harmonic distortion — how far the waveform deviates from a pure sine wave — typically measures under 3% on an inverter versus 15-25% on a conventional generator. Anything with a switching power supply or a microprocessor is happier on clean power: laptops, modern televisions, variable-speed appliance motors, CPAP machines, and battery chargers. Dirty power does not always destroy electronics immediately; it degrades them and causes erratic behavior.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Low Noise</h3>
          <p>
            Idling at 2,200 rpm instead of 3,600 makes an enormous audible difference, and inverter units are typically wrapped in sound-insulating enclosures on top of that. The best measure under 55 dB at light load; conventional portables run 68-76 dB constantly.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Fuel Efficiency</h3>
          <p>
